==============================================================================
(L1) S_g contains 4*Lambda; [Lambda:S_g] is a power of 2
==============================================================================
sigma=(1 2)                  eps=['1', '0', '0', '0', '0', '0', '0', '0']
                             2eps in L: True | (4eps,0,0) in Lambda: True | (4eps,0,0)*v = v*(4eps,0,0) = 4*swap23(v) on the basis: True
                             4*Lambda in S: True | 2*Lambda in S: True | [Lambda:S] = 65536
s_r, r=(e0+..+e6-e7)/2       eps=['3/4', '-1/4', '-1/4', '-1/4', '-1/4', '-1/4', '-1/4', '1/4']
                             2eps in L: True | (4eps,0,0) in Lambda: True | (4eps,0,0)*v = v*(4eps,0,0) = 4*swap23(v) on the basis: True
                             4*Lambda in S: True | 2*Lambda in S: True | [Lambda:S] = 1
3-cycle (5 6 7)              eps=['1', '0', '0', '0', '0', '0', '0', '0']
                             2eps in L: True | (4eps,0,0) in Lambda: True | (4eps,0,0)*v = v*(4eps,0,0) = 4*swap23(v) on the basis: True
                             4*Lambda in S: True | 2*Lambda in S: True | [Lambda:S] = 1024

==============================================================================
(L2) 2-adic factorisation [Lambda:S] = [B:B.B] [A:A.A]^2
==============================================================================
Lambda_D, Lambda_T inside Lambda: True
[Lambda : Lambda_D + Lambda_T] = 6561 = 3^8
Lambda cap D = Lambda_D and Lambda cap T = Lambda_T: (x,x,x) in Lambda iff x in L s; (x,y,-x-y) in Lambda iff x,y in L sbar  [checked on the 2L-cosets below]
   verified over all classes mod 2L: True True
sigma=(1 2)                  [B:B.B] = 1, [A:A.A] = 256  ->  [B:B.B]*[A:A.A]^2 = 65536 ; [Lambda:S] = 65536  MATCH
s_r, r=(e0+..+e6-e7)/2       [B:B.B] = 1, [A:A.A] = 1  ->  [B:B.B]*[A:A.A]^2 = 1 ; [Lambda:S] = 1  MATCH
3-cycle (5 6 7)              [B:B.B] = 1, [A:A.A] = 32  ->  [B:B.B]*[A:A.A]^2 = 1024 ; [Lambda:S] = 1024  MATCH

==============================================================================
(L3) sigma: S = Lambda_D + 2*Lambda ; s_r: S = Lambda
==============================================================================
sigma: HNF(S) == HNF(Lambda_D + 2 Lambda): True
3-cycle: HNF(S) == HNF(Lambda_D + {(x,y,-x-y): x,y in pi^{-1}(A.A)} + 2 Lambda): True

==============================================================================
(L4) mod-2 picture and ideal properties (standard product, A = g(L sbar), B = g(L s))
==============================================================================
sigma=(1 2)                  A: left ideal True, right ideal True; dim span(V.V) = 0 (dim V = 4); A.A inside 2A: True
                             B: left ideal False, right ideal False; dim span(W.W) = 4 (dim W = 4)
s_r, r=(e0+..+e6-e7)/2       A: left ideal False, right ideal True; dim span(V.V) = 4 (dim V = 4); A.A inside 2A: False
                             B: left ideal False, right ideal False; dim span(W.W) = 4 (dim W = 4)
3-cycle (5 6 7)              A: left ideal False, right ideal False; dim span(V.V) = 1 (dim V = 4); A.A inside 2A: False
                             B: left ideal False, right ideal False; dim span(W.W) = 4 (dim W = 4)

==============================================================================
(L5) the 120 root reflections, classified by <r,e0>, <r,s>, <r,sbar> (r up to sign)
==============================================================================
type       |<r,e0>|  |<r,s>|  |<r,sbar>|   outcome counts (one per +-r pair)
e0+-ej            1        0           1   {('index 2^16', '[A:A.A]=256', '[B:B.B]=1'): 7}
e0+-ej            1        1           0   {('no closure', '[A:A.A]=256', '[B:B.B]=None'): 7}
ei+-ej            0        0           0   {('index 2^16', '[A:A.A]=256', '[B:B.B]=1'): 21}
ei+-ej            0        1           1   {('no closure', '[A:A.A]=256', '[B:B.B]=None'): 21}
half-int        1/2        0         1/2   {('no closure', '[A:A.A]=1', '[B:B.B]=None'): 35}
half-int        1/2        1         1/2   {('index 2^0', '[A:A.A]=1', '[B:B.B]=1'): 21}
half-int        1/2        1         3/2   {('index 2^0', '[A:A.A]=1', '[B:B.B]=1'): 7}
half-int        1/2        2         3/2   {('no closure', '[A:A.A]=1', '[B:B.B]=None'): 1}
(the factorisation [Lambda:S] = [B:B.B][A:A.A]^2 was asserted for every closing reflection;
 [X:X.X] = None means X.X is not contained in X, i.e. X is not closed)
identity s_r(L sbar) = r.L (as lattices, r the left factor) holds for 120 of the 120 reflections, fails for 0
